helpFilenameFolderContent.message:
Folder and filename templates are configured in Settings. BatchShot automatically removes characters that the operating system cannot use in filenames.<br><strong>Folder:</strong> Use <code>/</code> to create nested directories, for example <code>BatchShot/<span class="hl-kw">{date}</span>/<span class="hl-kw">{host}</span></code>.<br><strong>Filename:</strong> The default is <code><span class="hl-kw">{index}</span>-<span class="hl-kw">{host}</span></code>; the exported extension is appended automatically.<br><ul><li><code>{index}</code>: three-digit sequence number, such as 001.</li><li><code>{total}</code>: total task count.</li><li><code>{host}</code> / <code>{domain}</code>: page host.</li><li><code>{title}</code>: page title.</li><li><code>{keyword}</code>: text item from template or search tasks.</li><li><code>{datetime}</code>, <code>{date}</code>, <code>{time}</code>, <code>{year}</code>, <code>{month}</code>, <code>{day}</code>: current time.</li><li><code>{folder}</code>: rendered download folder; <code>{url}</code>: page URL.</li></ul><pre><code>Folder: BatchShot/{date}/{host}
Filename: {index}-{keyword}-{title}
Datetime format: YYYY-MM-DD_HHmmss</code></pre>
